  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the clear best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile aggregation is the dominant design lever (+0.092 over singleprofile multimodal). However, we have no evidence on whether transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool for combining multiple profiles. This experiment (config_020) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings identical to config_018, cleanly isolating the effect of the aggregation strategy. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information single-variable test: if transformer substantially improves over avgpool, it reshapes the search toward transformer-based aggregation for all future encoder/fusion combinations; if it is comparable, we can deprioritize transformer and focus remaining budget on RNA/image encoder upgrades or fusion strategy."
}

